+# INP diagnostics
+
+The page loads the self-hosted `assets/inp-diagnostics.js`, built from
+`src/inp-diagnostics.js` using Google's `web-vitals/attribution` library.
+After editing the source, run `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile` and `pnpm build`.
+Commit the generated assets as well: the existing static server serves the
+repository directly, with no build step at startup.
+
+## Reporting
+
+Set the `inp-report-endpoint` meta tag's `content` in `index.html` to your real
+analytics collector URL. The collector must accept JSON encoded as a
+`text/plain` POST body. Reporting uses `sendBeacon`, with a keepalive fetch
+fallback when beacon queuing is unavailable or rejected. Cross-origin
+collectors need appropriate CORS configuration for the fetch fallback.
+Delivery is best effort; configure CSP `connect-src` to allow the collector.
+No collector or server route is included in this static site, so the empty
+setting sends no network reports.
+
+Alternatively, existing analytics can subscribe to the `inp-diagnostic`
+window event and read `event.detail`. Add `?inp-debug` to a page URL to log
+reports with `console.debug` and report changes to the INP candidate while
+interacting. Production reports when the page becomes hidden. This measures
+page-level INP, not a log of every slow interaction; no interaction means no
+INP report. Repeated reports with the same `id` update the same metric:
+store the latest `value`, rather than counting each report as another visit.
+The library manages page lifecycle and back/forward cache restores.
+
+## Interpreting a report
+
+All durations are in milliseconds. `rating` identifies good, needs-improvement,
+and poor INP. Start with `dominantPhase` and the three phase durations:
+
+- `inputDelay`: inspect work already blocking the main thread before handlers.
+- `processingDuration`: inspect the interaction's event handlers.
+- `presentationDelay`: inspect rendering, layout, and work before the next paint.
+
+`interactionTarget` uses stable `data-inp-target` labels on the page's links.
+Add static labels to future controls; otherwise only the tag name is reported.
+No element text, input values, query strings, or URL fragments are collected.
+
+Where Long Animation Frames are available, `longestScript` includes the script
+URL, function, source character position, invoker type, forced layout duration,
+and the phase it overlaps most. Rendering and script totals provide additional
+clues. These are correlations to investigate, not proof that one script caused
+the entire delay. A null `longestScript` means no script attribution was available,
+not that JavaScript was absent. Event Timing support is required to measure INP;
+unsupported browsers do nothing. Long Animation Frames are optional: phase
+timings remain useful without them.
